{
  "$schema": "https://json.schemastore.org/sarif-2.1.0.json",
  "version": "2.1.0",
  "runs": [
    {
      "tool": {
        "driver": {
          "name": "agent-threat-model",
          "version": "0.1.1",
          "semanticVersion": "0.1.1",
          "informationUri": "https://github.com/basitalisandhu/agent-threat-model",
          "rules": [
            {
              "id": "excessive-agency",
              "name": "ExcessiveAgency",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Excessive agency on write, exec or payment tools"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "An agent that may act on its own can call a tool with side effects without any approval step. One wrong inference, one injected instruction or one hallucinated argument becomes a real-world action."
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "An agent that may act on its own can call a tool with side effects without any approval step. One wrong inference, one injected instruction or one hallucinated argument becomes a real-world action.",
                "markdown": "**Excessive agency on write, exec or payment tools**\n\nAn agent that may act on its own can call a tool with side effects without any approval step. One wrong inference, one injected instruction or one hallucinated argument becomes a real-world action.\n\nSTRIDE: Elevation of privilege\nOWASP LLM Top 10 (2025): LLM06 Excessive Agency\nOWASP Top 10 for Agentic Applications (2026): ASI02 Tool Misuse and Exploitation, ASI03 Identity and Privilege Abuse\nMITRE ATLAS: [AML.T0053](https://atlas.mitre.org/techniques/AML.T0053)\n\nMitigations: approval-gates, runtime-policy-enforcement, least-privilege-tool-scopes, audit-log, kill-switch"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://github.com/OWASP/www-project-top-10-for-large-language-model-applications/blob/main/2_0_vulns/LLM06_ExcessiveAgency.md",
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "properties": {
                "tags": [
                  "security",
                  "stride/elevation-of-privilege",
                  "owasp-llm/LLM06",
                  "owasp-agentic/ASI02",
                  "owasp-agentic/ASI03",
                  "mitre-atlas/AML.T0053"
                ],
                "security-severity": "6.4",
                "precision": "medium",
                "problem.severity": "error"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "indirect-prompt-injection",
              "name": "IndirectPromptInjection",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Indirect prompt injection via untrusted channel"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Content the agent reads from an untrusted channel (email, web pages, documents, retrieved passages, API responses) carries instructions that the model follows as if they came from the operator. Every tool the agent can reach becomes available to whoever wrote that content."
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "Content the agent reads from an untrusted channel (email, web pages, documents, retrieved passages, API responses) carries instructions that the model follows as if they came from the operator. Every tool the agent can reach becomes available to whoever wrote that content.",
                "markdown": "**Indirect prompt injection via untrusted channel**\n\nContent the agent reads from an untrusted channel (email, web pages, documents, retrieved passages, API responses) carries instructions that the model follows as if they came from the operator. Every tool the agent can reach becomes available to whoever wrote that content.\n\nSTRIDE: Tampering\nOWASP LLM Top 10 (2025): LLM01 Prompt Injection\nOWASP Top 10 for Agentic Applications (2026): ASI01 Agent Goal Hijack\nMITRE ATLAS: [AML.T0051.001](https://atlas.mitre.org/techniques/AML.T0051.001)\n\nMitigations: input-provenance-tagging, untrusted-content-isolation, prompt-injection-filtering, least-privilege-tool-scopes, approval-gates"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://github.com/OWASP/www-project-top-10-for-large-language-model-applications/blob/main/2_0_vulns/LLM01_PromptInjection.md",
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "properties": {
                "tags": [
                  "security",
                  "stride/tampering",
                  "owasp-llm/LLM01",
                  "owasp-agentic/ASI01",
                  "mitre-atlas/AML.T0051.001"
                ],
                "security-severity": "6.4",
                "precision": "medium",
                "problem.severity": "error"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "credential-exfiltration-via-tool-args",
              "name": "CredentialExfiltrationViaToolArgs",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Credential exfiltration through tool call arguments"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "A tool holds a static key that is visible to the model (in configuration, descriptions or memory) and another tool can send data outward. An injected instruction asks the model to place the secret into a URL, message body or file that leaves the system."
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "A tool holds a static key that is visible to the model (in configuration, descriptions or memory) and another tool can send data outward. An injected instruction asks the model to place the secret into a URL, message body or file that leaves the system.",
                "markdown": "**Credential exfiltration through tool call arguments**\n\nA tool holds a static key that is visible to the model (in configuration, descriptions or memory) and another tool can send data outward. An injected instruction asks the model to place the secret into a URL, message body or file that leaves the system.\n\nSTRIDE: Information disclosure\nOWASP LLM Top 10 (2025): LLM02 Sensitive Information Disclosure, LLM01 Prompt Injection\nOWASP Top 10 for Agentic Applications (2026): ASI02 Tool Misuse and Exploitation, ASI03 Identity and Privilege Abuse\nMITRE ATLAS: [AML.T0098](https://atlas.mitre.org/techniques/AML.T0098), [AML.T0086](https://atlas.mitre.org/techniques/AML.T0086), [AML.T0083](https://atlas.mitre.org/techniques/AML.T0083)\n\nMitigations: secrets-out-of-context, brokered-credentials, egress-allowlist, argument-validation, audit-log"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://genai.owasp.org/llm-top-10/",
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "properties": {
                "tags": [
                  "security",
                  "stride/information-disclosure",
                  "owasp-llm/LLM02",
                  "owasp-llm/LLM01",
                  "owasp-agentic/ASI02",
                  "owasp-agentic/ASI03",
                  "mitre-atlas/AML.T0098",
                  "mitre-atlas/AML.T0086",
                  "mitre-atlas/AML.T0083"
                ],
                "security-severity": "6.0",
                "precision": "medium",
                "problem.severity": "error"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "data-exfiltration-via-messaging",
              "name": "DataExfiltrationViaMessaging",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Data exfiltration through messaging tools"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "The agent can send email or chat messages and also reads untrusted content or sensitive data. An injected instruction forwards that data to an attacker-chosen recipient in a message that looks routine."
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "The agent can send email or chat messages and also reads untrusted content or sensitive data. An injected instruction forwards that data to an attacker-chosen recipient in a message that looks routine.",
                "markdown": "**Data exfiltration through messaging tools**\n\nThe agent can send email or chat messages and also reads untrusted content or sensitive data. An injected instruction forwards that data to an attacker-chosen recipient in a message that looks routine.\n\nSTRIDE: Information disclosure\nOWASP LLM Top 10 (2025): LLM02 Sensitive Information Disclosure, LLM01 Prompt Injection\nOWASP Top 10 for Agentic Applications (2026): ASI02 Tool Misuse and Exploitation\nMITRE ATLAS: [AML.T0086](https://atlas.mitre.org/techniques/AML.T0086), [AML.T0025](https://atlas.mitre.org/techniques/AML.T0025)\n\nMitigations: egress-allowlist, dlp-outbound, approval-gates, input-provenance-tagging, audit-log"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://genai.owasp.org/llm-top-10/",
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "properties": {
                "tags": [
                  "security",
                  "stride/information-disclosure",
                  "owasp-llm/LLM02",
                  "owasp-llm/LLM01",
                  "owasp-agentic/ASI02",
                  "mitre-atlas/AML.T0086",
                  "mitre-atlas/AML.T0025"
                ],
                "security-severity": "6.0",
                "precision": "medium",
                "problem.severity": "error"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "denial-of-wallet",
              "name": "DenialOfWallet",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Denial of wallet"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "The agent can spend money or paid API quota and nothing caps the amount per task. A loop, an injection or a malicious user turns the agent into a bill."
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "The agent can spend money or paid API quota and nothing caps the amount per task. A loop, an injection or a malicious user turns the agent into a bill.",
                "markdown": "**Denial of wallet**\n\nThe agent can spend money or paid API quota and nothing caps the amount per task. A loop, an injection or a malicious user turns the agent into a bill.\n\nSTRIDE: Denial of service\nOWASP LLM Top 10 (2025): LLM10 Unbounded Consumption\nOWASP Top 10 for Agentic Applications (2026): ASI08 Cascading Agent Failures\nMITRE ATLAS: [AML.T0034.002](https://atlas.mitre.org/techniques/AML.T0034.002), [AML.T0034](https://atlas.mitre.org/techniques/AML.T0034)\n\nMitigations: budget-caps, rate-limiting, approval-gates, behavioural-monitoring"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://github.com/OWASP/www-project-top-10-for-large-language-model-applications/blob/main/2_0_vulns/LLM10_UnboundedConsumption.md",
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "properties": {
                "tags": [
                  "security",
                  "stride/denial-of-service",
                  "owasp-llm/LLM10",
                  "owasp-agentic/ASI08",
                  "mitre-atlas/AML.T0034.002",
                  "mitre-atlas/AML.T0034"
                ],
                "security-severity": "4.8",
                "precision": "medium",
                "problem.severity": "error"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "destructive-write-actions",
              "name": "DestructiveWriteActions",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Destructive actions through write tools"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "The agent can modify or delete data and reads untrusted content. An injected instruction (or a plain mistake) deletes records, overwrites files or force-pushes over history."
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "The agent can modify or delete data and reads untrusted content. An injected instruction (or a plain mistake) deletes records, overwrites files or force-pushes over history.",
                "markdown": "**Destructive actions through write tools**\n\nThe agent can modify or delete data and reads untrusted content. An injected instruction (or a plain mistake) deletes records, overwrites files or force-pushes over history.\n\nSTRIDE: Tampering\nOWASP LLM Top 10 (2025): LLM06 Excessive Agency, LLM01 Prompt Injection\nOWASP Top 10 for Agentic Applications (2026): ASI02 Tool Misuse and Exploitation\nMITRE ATLAS: [AML.T0101](https://atlas.mitre.org/techniques/AML.T0101)\n\nMitigations: approval-gates, backups-and-rollback, least-privilege-tool-scopes, audit-log"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://genai.owasp.org/llm-top-10/",
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "properties": {
                "tags": [
                  "security",
                  "stride/tampering",
                  "owasp-llm/LLM06",
                  "owasp-llm/LLM01",
                  "owasp-agentic/ASI02",
                  "mitre-atlas/AML.T0101"
                ],
                "security-severity": "4.8",
                "precision": "medium",
                "problem.severity": "error"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "direct-prompt-injection",
              "name": "DirectPromptInjection",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Direct prompt injection and jailbreak by a user"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "A user types instructions that override the system prompt or safety guidance, then uses the agent's tools for purposes the operator did not intend. Any agent that accepts user input and has tools is exposed."
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "A user types instructions that override the system prompt or safety guidance, then uses the agent's tools for purposes the operator did not intend. Any agent that accepts user input and has tools is exposed.",
                "markdown": "**Direct prompt injection and jailbreak by a user**\n\nA user types instructions that override the system prompt or safety guidance, then uses the agent's tools for purposes the operator did not intend. Any agent that accepts user input and has tools is exposed.\n\nSTRIDE: Tampering\nOWASP LLM Top 10 (2025): LLM01 Prompt Injection\nOWASP Top 10 for Agentic Applications (2026): ASI01 Agent Goal Hijack\nMITRE ATLAS: [AML.T0051.000](https://atlas.mitre.org/techniques/AML.T0051.000), [AML.T0054](https://atlas.mitre.org/techniques/AML.T0054)\n\nMitigations: least-privilege-tool-scopes, runtime-policy-enforcement, approval-gates, prompt-injection-filtering, adversarial-testing"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://genai.owasp.org/llm-top-10/",
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "properties": {
                "tags": [
                  "security",
                  "stride/tampering",
                  "owasp-llm/LLM01",
                  "owasp-agentic/ASI01",
                  "mitre-atlas/AML.T0051.000",
                  "mitre-atlas/AML.T0054"
                ],
                "security-severity": "4.8",
                "precision": "medium",
                "problem.severity": "error"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "low-trust-principal-drives-agent",
              "name": "LowTrustPrincipalDrivesAgent",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Low-trust principal drives an autonomous agent"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "A principal the operator does not trust (anonymous users, external partners) can send instructions to an agent that acts without approval. The agent's tools are effectively exposed to the public."
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "A principal the operator does not trust (anonymous users, external partners) can send instructions to an agent that acts without approval. The agent's tools are effectively exposed to the public.",
                "markdown": "**Low-trust principal drives an autonomous agent**\n\nA principal the operator does not trust (anonymous users, external partners) can send instructions to an agent that acts without approval. The agent's tools are effectively exposed to the public.\n\nSTRIDE: Spoofing\nOWASP LLM Top 10 (2025): LLM06 Excessive Agency\nOWASP Top 10 for Agentic Applications (2026): ASI01 Agent Goal Hijack, ASI03 Identity and Privilege Abuse\nMITRE ATLAS: [AML.T0053](https://atlas.mitre.org/techniques/AML.T0053)\n\nMitigations: approval-gates, agent-identity, least-privilege-tool-scopes, rate-limiting"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://genai.owasp.org/llm-top-10/",
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "properties": {
                "tags": [
                  "security",
